[Genre / Era]
Late-1960s art-folk / psychedelic space ballad with early glam undertones.
British art-rock sensibility. Intimate, cinematic, melancholic.

[Tempo & Meter]
~64–68 BPM
4/4, slow pulse, floating feel
Tempo should feel unmoored, emotionally suspended

[Harmony & Tonality]
Centered in C major / A minor ambiguity
Frequent use of IV → V → I resolution delayed or avoided
Suspended chords, added 9ths, gentle modal color
Harmonic movement feels like drifting, not traveling

[Structure (Narrative Form)]
Verse-led storytelling, not chorus-driven
Refrain appears as an emotional checkpoint, not a hook
Ending dissolves rather than resolves

[Instrumentation]
Acoustic guitar (fingerpicked, intimate, close-mic)
Mellotron or analog string pad (soft, slightly unstable)
Sparse piano accents (felt or upright tone)
Minimal bass, warm and rounded
Drums enter late (brushes or soft kit, heartbeat-level)
Subtle analog synth sweeps suggesting zero gravity

[Vocal Direction]
Solo male vocal
Gentle British phrasing, emotionally detached but fragile
Close-mic, audible breath, slight saturation
Delivery feels like reporting emotions, not performing them
Occasional harmony lines that feel distant, like radio chatter

[Production Texture]
1969 analog warmth
Slight tape wobble
Stereo width used sparingly
Reverb feels cosmic, long tail, but low in mix
Silence and space are intentional

[Emotional Physics]
Awe → isolation → quiet acceptance
No triumph
No panic
Calm loneliness

[Conceptual Core]
A lone human voice communicating from a fragile place between wonder and disappearance.
Technology fades. Emotion remains.

[Lyrics]
Verse 1

Ground control, I hear you clear
Your signal hums, but feels so far
Panels glow, the world goes small
Earth is just a quiet star

Pre-Refrain

Counting seconds in my chest
Every breath is borrowed air
I was trained to know the math
No one taught me how to care

Refrain

And I’m floating where the answers fade
Between the dark and light
If I lose the pull of home tonight
Tell them I was calm in flight

Verse 2

Windows show a curved goodbye
Clouds like thoughts I couldn’t keep
All the words I meant to say
Drift like tools I couldn’t reach

Bridge

There’s no sound where I’m becoming
Just the echo of my name
If this silence is forever
It’s a beautiful way to change

Final Refrain / Outro

I’m not lost, just out of view
Past the maps you’re holding tight
If you look into the dark long enough
You might see me pass the light